# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
venv/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# GitReins sandbox (evaluation scratch space)
.gitreins-sandbox/
# GitReins guard history (runtime artifacts, no versioning needed)
.gitreins/history/
# Reaped-worktree preservation bundles (worktree-hygiene.py writes
# .gitreins/rescued-<date>/<tree>/ before every removal — same class as
# `history/` above: durable on-disk evidence, never versioned). Without this
# rule every reap leaves ~30 permanently-untracked paths that read as an
# ownership barrier to each subsequent lane tick.
.gitreins/rescued-*/
# Judge token-usage telemetry (PR #2 — best-effort cost log, never committed)
.gitreins/usage.jsonl
# Guard run logs (DF-018 — one full, untruncated log per guard run; runtime
# artifacts, pruned to the newest GUARD_LOG_KEEP runs)
.gitreins/logs/
# QA run ledger (gitreins qa — one row per QA run; runtime artifact. Point
# GITREINS_QA_LEDGER at a tracked path to version it.)
.gitreins/qa-ledger.jsonl
# Runtime task data (committed separately on gitreins branch)
.gitreins/tasks.yaml
# Dated backup strays a writer leaves beside a GitReins store (QA-GITREINS-POC-1
# residual: `.gitignore` covered the store but not `<store>.bak.<epoch>`).
.gitreins/tasks.yaml.bak.*
.gitreins/*.bak.*

# Secrets
.env
*.key
*.pem

# Test artifacts
.coverage
.skylos/
# Node (if present from bootstrap)
node_modules/
apps/
packages/
temporal-vector/
# Temp
test_write
*.tmp
*.db

# Cross-project artifacts (not part of GitReins)
category-mapping.yaml
hivemind-audit.md

# GitReins nested runtime artifacts
.gitreins/.gitreins/
.gitreins/worktrees.json
.gitreins/worktrees.lock
.gitreins/disposable.json
.gitreins/disposable.lock
# DF-GITREINS-POC-47: the task store's flock sidecar. The `.gitreins/*.lock`
# rule further down already covers it; it is listed literally because the
# installer template (gitreins.cli.GITREINS_GITIGNORE_ENTRIES) is pinned to
# this file entry-for-entry by tests/test_cli.py
# (test_vendor_gitignore_covers_every_template_entry).
.gitreins/tasks.yaml.lock
.gitreins/config.yaml.bak
# DF-GITREINS-POC-48: the merge-gate verdict document an ephemeral judge run
# writes when asked (`judge --ephemeral --persist-verdict`). Runtime artifact,
# not history — `.gitreins/history/` above stays the durable record.
.gitreins/verdicts/
# DF-GITREINS-POC-96: the repo-produced quality artifact. The artifact contract
# (docs/quality-metrics.md) stamps `produced_at` provenance on every run that
# reads the snapshot, so a conforming producer rewrites it every guard/judge/
# doctor run. Ignored by default; git keeps versioning an already-tracked copy.
.gitreins/quality.json
.gitreins/review-state.json
.gitreins/review-state.lock
.gitreins/review-state.corrupt-*
.gitreins/review-state.recovery-required

# Hilo — the code graph is DERIVED state and is not committed (GR-225).
#
# `edges.jsonl` and the DuckDB cache hilo builds from it used to ship in git so a
# clone could answer cold. Measured cost of that choice: a shipped index is frozen
# at the commit that produced it, so every module added afterwards is invisible —
# a clone of HEAD indexed 32 of 53 tracked `engine/*.py` modules and carried no
# mention of `engine/preflight.py` at all, so the pre-dispatch gate graded a
# tracked module `missing` (evidence_quality 1, REVIEW) on every fresh clone, CI
# runner and ephemeral install. `gitreins resolve` now bootstraps the index
# itself when it is absent or stale (`ensure_graph_index` in
# engine/resolution.py), so a clone pays ONE warm instead of inheriting a lie.
#
# Keep this list in step with what hilo writes under `.vfs/`. This file is
# TRACKED, and `hilo init` APPENDS its managed block whenever its MARKER line is
# absent — so an omission does not merely leave untracked dirt during the
# bootstrap, it edits a tracked file in the consumer's checkout. The block below
# is hilo's own, verbatim and marker included, for exactly that reason.
# --- hilo managed: rebuildable .vfs cache state (installed by `hilo init`) ---
.vfs/graph/graph.db
.vfs/graph/graph.db.wal
.vfs/graph/graph.duckdb
.vfs/graph/graph.duckdb.wal
.vfs/graph/.last_warm
.vfs/graph/.parse_cache.json
.vfs/graph/.symbols_cache.json
.vfs/graph/.last_reconcile
# hilo's prelude entry for the derived cache — kept so `hilo init` does not
# append its prelude either; the edge index itself is NOT committed (see above).
.vfs/graph/graph.db*
# The index itself plus the query caches sqlite/duckdb leave behind (GR-225).
# GR-193: the symbols cache is writer output too — the post-commit/post-merge
# hooks run `hilo graph warm --changed`, which rewrites it after every commit,
# so a tracked copy re-dirtied a clean tree in every worktree (it is inside
# hilo's managed block above now).
.vfs/graph/*.db
.vfs/graph/*.db.wal
.vfs/graph/edges.jsonl
.vfs/graph/edges.jsonl.lock
.vfs/graph/state.json
.vfs/graph/coverage.json
# The warm record `ensure_graph_index` writes: which HEAD the local index was
# built at (the staleness signal for the next resolve).
.vfs/graph/.gitreins_index.json
# `hilo init` writes this project manifest; its `project.name` is this
# checkout's directory name — machine-local, not repo config.
.vfs/manifest.yaml

# Demo projects (own git repos, not part of GitReins source)
demo-calc/
demo-slugify/

# Board JSONL canonical store (5b6df60/JSONL-NORM-001) — cache binaries untracked; JSONL files are the tracked store

.coding-hermes/board/board.db
.coding-hermes/board/board.db.wal
.coding-hermes/board/*.parquet
.coding-hermes/board/*.duckdb

# Runtime locks are never committed: two agents holding one at once produce a tracked
# conflict on a file that carries no information (REVIEW-006).
.gitreins/*.lock
.coding-hermes/board/.lock

# Embedded DuckBrain namespace store: a nested git repo. Tracked as an accidental
# gitlink by the GR-146 sweep (48d7f7b); it made the tree unclonable and fails the
# GR-153 authoritative-fingerprint preflight (state gitlink), so verdict persistence
# refuses. The store stays on disk, outside git's view.
namespaces/coding-hermes/
